WHY THIS LICENCE, AND WHAT ATTRIBUTION MEANS HERE

CC BY is not a stylistic choice. The canal geometry this study is built on
was published by someone else under CC BY, so the attribution chain has to
be carried forward rather than closed off. Reusing the files under DATA/ or
results/ therefore means crediting two things:

  1. This package, as given in CITATION.cff.

  2. The source of the canal geometry:

     Bonet, E.; Yubero, M. T.; Bascompta, M.; Alfonso, P. (2025).
     A Linear Model for Irrigation Canals Operating in Real Time Applied
     in ASCE Test Cases. Water 17(9):1368.
     https://doi.org/10.3390/w17091368
     Licensed CC BY. Tables 5 and 6.

     Target depths are taken from:

     Litrico, X.; Fromion, V. (2004). Simplified Modeling of Irrigation
     Canals for Controller Design. Journal of Irrigation and Drainage
     Engineering 130(5):373-383.
     https://doi.org/10.1061/(ASCE)0733-9437(2004)130:5(373)

DATA/inputs.json carries these citations beside the numbers they apply to,
together with a provenance label for every block: observed, derived, or
assumed. The labels are not decoration. "Observed" means somebody else
published it and the citation travels with it; "derived" means it follows
from something observed by a stated formula; "assumed" means this study
chose it because no published value was found. Anyone reusing these files
should keep the labels with the numbers, because a value whose provenance
has been stripped cannot be checked by the next person.
